                <invention-title lang="de">SYSTEME UND VERFAHREN ZUR INTEGRATION VON PATIENTENDRUCK IN DIE ABGABE EINER MEDIZINISCHEN FLÜSSIGKEIT</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">SYSTÈMES ET PROCÉDÉS POUR INCORPORER UNE PRESSION DE PATIENT DANS UNE ADMINISTRATION DE FLUIDE MÉDICAL</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">SYSTEMS AND METHODS FOR INCORPORATING PATIENT PRESSURE INTO MEDICAL FLUID DELIVERY</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A medical fluid delivery system (110) is described. The system comprises: a medical fluid handling device (170) including a patient line (116) for being placed in fluid communication with a patient; and a medical fluid delivery machine (120) including a pump actuator (126) for actuating the medical fluid handling device to move medical fluid into or out of the device, a pressure sensor positioned and arranged within the medical fluid handling device and configured to sense pressure of the medical fluid, and a control unit (160) in signal communication with the pressure sensor and control communication with the pump actuator, the control unit programmed to perform a routine during pumping in which the control unit (i) determines when at least one signal reading or a component of the at least one signal reading from the pressure sensor is indicative of a pressure within the patient, and (ii) determines from the at least one pressure signal reading or component reading indicative of the pressure in the patient whether to continue pumping or stop pumping.</p>
            </abstract>
